- Other workflows handle Meta/LinkedIn engagement, content intelligence, SEO/GEO, token health, Telegram, video pilots/layers, deployments and marketplace.

ROOT CAUSES / REMEDIATIONS
1. Blogger OAuth invalid_grant: external credential issue. The Google OAuth owner must verify consent-screen mode, re-authorize with Blogger scope and update GitHub secret BLOGGER_OAUTH_JSON. Code cannot revive a revoked token. Do not share the secret.
2. Blogger label error: fixed by normalize_blogger_labels() across REST/UI paths, with regression tests; combined label length is capped below Blogger's 200-character limit.
3. Gemini 429: model-name cycling shares the same project quota. Blogger demand worker now skips Gemini if no key, stops model cycling on quota errors and uses the verified-source fallback. The fallback must remain conservative.
4. Reel timeout: root cause was looped still-image inputs without a hard output cap. Main and fallback overlays now include source-duration -t and -shortest. Run 38055595685 confirms the 69.8-second Reel reached Telegram.
5. Pharaonic imagery: generation uses a positive post-derived contemporary scene; final QA now explicitly checks period-style mismatch. Provider, prompt and final-file hash are logged to sidecar; QA outcome is appended. Exact published image must still be reviewed.
6. Cross-workflow artifacts: artifacts are scoped to workflow runs. Do not assume another workflow can see them. Use durable committed source context or explicit run ID/token.
7. UI success: dialog closure is not publication proof. Require exact title Published state and public feed/dashboard permalink; Google HTML search is unreliable due 429.

SECRET NAMES ONLY
Potential workflow secret names: BLOGGER_OAUTH_JSON, BLOGGER_UI_STORAGE_STATE_B64, BLOGGER_BLOG_ID, BLOGGER_URL, BLOGGER_ENABLED, GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON, GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS, GOOGLE_SHEET_URL, GOOGLE_SHEET_ID, GOOGLE_SHEET_RANGE, GEMINI_API_KEY, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID, Cloudflare account/token secrets, and platform-specific Meta/LinkedIn tokens. Never record values.

